\cf0 <p class="lead">Varley sells quiet confidence, and the store earns it \'97 the photography, the tone, the restraint are all right. So the brief here isn't a mass-market conversion checklist; bolting on star widgets, countdown timers and progress meters would actively cheapen a brand at this tier. The opportunity is to close real friction <strong>in the brand's own register</strong>: the product page gives a shopper a price before a single reason to want it, there's no fit reassurance where size doubt lives, navigation offers a 170-piece wardrobe only four routes in, and almost nothing helps a shopper build the outfit the imagery already styles. Every recommendation below is designed to read as Varley, not as a discount store borrowing its tactics.</p>\cell \row

